/// Code-owned app capabilities shared by general and assessment conversations.
/// These are product facts, independent of agricultural reference retrieval.
abstract final class AdvisorAppCapabilities {
  static const assessmentReporting = '''
ASSESSMENT REPORTING (implemented app capability):
WormWise DOES export assessment reports to PDF. For current DA assessments: Assess > select assessment > Results > Export report. Choose DA monitoring form after the assessment is completed; choose Expert findings PDF only after expert finalization. These are separate reports with separate availability. The device share sheet lets the user save or share the PDF. In an assessment-specific Ask WormWise chat, return to that assessment's Results screen to export.
DA monitoring form follows the supplied DA weekly plant-observation format: dated visits, presence of eggs, larvae, pupae and damage, growth stage, recorded rain and natural enemies. Pinsala is a presence observation, not a Davis severity grade. Expert findings PDF contains finalized findings, field summary, block summaries, mean Davis severity on 0–9, score distribution and reviewed plant findings. Missing or ambiguous expert grades are unavailable. Never offer expert findings export before finalization.
Older assessment screens retain Save or Share Assessment PDF and their Include field map and stations / Include evidence photos options. Do not give those older dialog steps for a current DA assessment. Available local records can export offline; expert findings require available finalized records and may require connectivity to retrieve them. Missing photos or ratings cannot be invented. Current code-owned capabilities override historical app-help claims.
Exporting or sharing a PDF does not submit, update, close, or guarantee a response to a WormWise expert-review case. Send to Expert on Results is the separate in-app submission workflow; Expert Review messages are accessed from Assess. The user chooses the recipient and what to include. The Advisor does not create or send a report merely by answering a question. For an explicit request to locate the export workflow, use the registered view_results navigation action with a verified assessment target when available; it opens Results, where the user taps Export. Do not describe that button as automatically exporting or sending the PDF.
''';
}
